1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,122
This is the Aedes aegypti,

2
00:00:03,122 --> 00:00:05,245
it transmits the dengue virus.

3
00:00:05,245 --> 00:00:07,368
The Aedes albopictus,

4
00:00:07,368 --> 00:00:09,490
better known as the tiger mosquito,

5
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:11,613
can also transmit dengue.

6
00:00:11,613 --> 00:00:13,736
Female Aedes lay their eggs

7
00:00:13,736 --> 00:00:15,858
in standing water.

8
00:00:15,858 --> 00:00:17,981
An egg takes between 7 and 10 days

9
00:00:17,981 --> 00:00:20,104
to become an adult mosquito.

10
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:23,419
Without any control measures,

11
00:00:23,419 --> 00:00:25,339
dengue is passed to humans

12
00:00:25,339 --> 00:00:27,259
through mosquito bites.

13
00:00:27,259 --> 00:00:29,179
Only females bite humans,

14
00:00:29,179 --> 00:00:31,099
as they need blood

15
00:00:31,099 --> 00:00:33,019
for their eggs to develop.

16
00:00:33,019 --> 00:00:34,939
Dengue symptoms include high fever,

17
00:00:34,939 --> 00:00:36,859
intense headache, body aches,

18
00:00:36,859 --> 00:00:38,779
and red spots on the skin.

19
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,950
With individual measures,

20
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:44,100
such as repellent, long clothing,

21
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,251
and mosquito nets,

22
00:00:46,251 --> 00:00:48,401
some people can protect themselves.

23
00:00:48,401 --> 00:00:50,552
But other measures can help too.

24
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:54,031
Collective measures make

25
00:00:54,031 --> 00:00:55,762
a big difference!

26
00:00:55,762 --> 00:00:57,493
Vaccines, when available,

27
00:00:57,493 --> 00:00:59,224
protect people even when bitten.

28
00:00:59,224 --> 00:01:00,955
Insecticides reduce

29
00:01:00,955 --> 00:01:02,686
the mosquito population.

30
00:01:02,686 --> 00:01:04,417
The combination of different measures

31
00:01:04,417 --> 00:01:06,148
strengthens the fight

32
00:01:06,148 --> 00:01:07,880
against the disease.

33
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,652
When we take care of the environment,

34
00:01:10,652 --> 00:01:12,404
removing rubbish,

35
00:01:12,404 --> 00:01:14,156
covering water containers,

36
00:01:14,156 --> 00:01:15,908
and eliminating breeding sites,

37
00:01:15,908 --> 00:01:17,660
mosquitoes lose them

38
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,412
and have no place to lay their eggs

39
00:01:19,412 --> 00:01:21,164
and develop into adults!

40
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:25,619
The environment makes

41
00:01:25,619 --> 00:01:27,638
all the difference.

42
00:01:27,638 --> 00:01:29,658
Rain and discarded waste together

43
00:01:29,658 --> 00:01:31,677
produce more breeding sites.

44
00:01:31,677 --> 00:01:33,697
Cleaning and care eliminates them.

45
00:01:33,697 --> 00:01:35,716
In dense urban areas,

46
00:01:35,716 --> 00:01:37,736
the risk is even greater.

47
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,642
The same mosquitoes that transmit

48
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:42,485
dengue also transmit

49
00:01:42,485 --> 00:01:44,328
Zika and chikungunya.

50
00:01:44,328 --> 00:01:46,170
But with knowledge

51
00:01:46,170 --> 00:01:48,013
and collective action,

52
00:01:48,013 --> 00:01:49,856
we can win this battle.

53
00:01:49,856 --> 00:01:51,698
Protect yourself.

54
00:01:51,698 --> 00:01:53,541
Protect your community.

55
00:01:53,541 --> 00:01:55,384
Take care of the environment.

